<headroom-library version="1" id="crunch-southern-twin-lead" category="Crunch" order="90" instrument="guitar" style="Southern Rock">
  <description>Humbuckers into a 50-watt British head with its channels jumped and run hot: a sweet, vocal mid-gain lead that stays clear in harmony lines, with a hint of echo and room. Guitar volume on 10 for leads, back it off for chunky rhythm.</description>
  <tags><tag>Crunch</tag><tag>Southern Rock</tag><tag>Classic Rock</tag><tag>Lead</tag><tag>Humbucker</tag><tag>Delay</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://www.guitarplayer.com/players/classic-tones-statesboro-blues-the-allman-brothers" title="Guitar Player: Classic Tones, 'Statesboro Blues' (The Allman Brothers Band)"/>
    <source url="https://allmanbrothersband.com/10-things-y-gotta-do-to-play-like-duane-allman/" title="AllmanBrothersBand.com: 10 things y' gotta do to play like Duane Allman"/>
    <source url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duane_Allman" title="Duane Allman (Wikipedia)"/>
    <source url="https://blog.zzounds.com/2018/03/17/legends-tone-the-allman-brothers-band/" title="zZounds blog: Legends of Tone, The Allman Brothers Band"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
